  "response_text": "If we don\u2019t set the PSP to point to the prepared thread stack, the CPU would use an invalid or garbage value when trying to load register data for the new thread. This leads to memory access violations or trying to execute junk code, which causes a hard fault. By setting PSP to the top of the stack we set up, we make sure that the CPU loads proper values into registers and begins executing the thread safely.\\n",
